  "recommendation": {
    "mechanism": "S5",
    "in_process": false,
    "summary": "S5 FD-passing process handoff with identity state transfer (new binary).",
    "justification": [
      "goroutine-structure, long-running or start-up code changed: in-process patching would leave old code running in goroutines that never return; a new process starts the new goroutine structure, and the old one is drained and exits",
      "S6 blockers (8): github.com/gotify/server/v2/api.generateApplicationToken: type of a package-level variable changed; github.com/gotify/server/v2/api.generateClientToken: type of a package-level variable changed; github.com/gotify/server/v2/api/stream.writeJSON: package-level initializer ran once at start-up; S6 patches functions, not data; github.com/gotify/server/v2/auth.Auth.handleClient: closures created before the patch (e.g. middleware chains built at start-up) keep the old code; only newly created closures see the fix; github.com/gotify/server/v2/auth.tokenCharacters: package-level initializer ran once at start-up; S6 patches functions, not data; ... and 3 more"
    ],
    "alternatives": [
      "Kubernetes rolling update (loses in-memory state, needs surge capacity)"
    ],
    "risks": [
      "github.com/gotify/server/v2/auth.GenerateApplicationToken is exported: callers outside the analysed module are not in the closure",
      "github.com/gotify/server/v2/auth.GenerateClientToken is exported: callers outside the analysed module are not in the closure",
      "github.com/gotify/server/v2/auth.GenerateNotExistingToken is exported: callers outside the analysed module are not in the closure",
      "new package-level variable github.com/gotify/server/v2/auth.enhancedTokenPrefix: under S6 it lives in the patch plugin and is re-initialised by every later patch generation",
      "new package-level variable github.com/gotify/server/v2/auth.errCannotParseToken: under S6 it lives in the patch plugin and is re-initialised by every later patch generation",
      "new package-level variable github.com/gotify/server/v2/auth.errInvalidToken: under S6 it lives in the patch plugin and is re-initialised by every later patch generation",
      "new package-level variable github.com/gotify/server/v2/auth.errNoPrivateKey: under S6 it lives in the patch plugin and is re-initialised by every later patch generation",
      "github.com/gotify/server/v2/test.Tokens is exported: callers outside the analysed module are not in the closure",
      "changed functions are small enough to be inlined; with S6 slot trampolines the call still dispatches through the slot, but raw binary patching (internal/livepatch) must also patch the inlining callers: github.com/gotify/server/v2/api.supportOrAbort, github.com/gotify/server/v2/plugin.Manager.initializeSingleUserPlugin, github.com/gotify/server/v2/router.Create, github.com/gotify/server/v2/runner.startListening",
      "no patched function has a context.Context parameter: S6 gives per-call (not per-request) consistency, so one request may mix old and new versions of the 25 functions",
      "1 patched functions are in package main; a Go plugin cannot import package main, so hotpatchgen must relocate them into an importable package",
      "type information is partial (352/352 type errors old/new; third-party packages are opaque): call-graph and state reachability are lower bounds",
      "quiescence: old activations of main(), init-started or long-running goroutines never return, so the old process is retired by exit, not by draining; set a drain deadline in the S5 upgrader"
    ]
  },
